# tools/click_between_witness.rish -- the THREE-CLICK BETWEENNESS relation on metal: turn THREE points into THREE whole-group selections (two ENDPOINT
# taps and one MIDDLE-candidate tap), then read whether the middle group sits BETWEEN the endpoints in the reading SEQUENCE and in SPACE, lifting the
# click family's ternary arity one step past image/click_nearest.rye through image/click_order.rye and image/click_bounds.rye (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/click_nearest.rye reads which of two candidates is NEARER an anchor. This rung reads whether a candidate is
# BETWEEN two others. image/hit_test.rye names the ONE object under a point, image/overlap_clusters.rye's cluster_of names the connected group,
# image/click_order.rye's click_group_min_rank reads a group's page rank, image/click_bounds.rye's click_bbox reads a group's handle frame. A reading
# over readings -- no plane of its own, no pixel written.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: reading-order betweenness and spatial betweenness are DIFFERENT relations that differ in KIND. A group can read
# between two others yet lie outside their span box (order_only), or lie inside their span box yet read outside them (space_only); the reading order is a
# total order so exactly one of any three groups is the reading-middle, while the plane is only partial so a triple can have NO spatial middle at all.
# Over six singleton objects (P rank 1, V a tall block rank 2, W rank 3, Q rank 4, S rank 5, R rank 6): P/Q/R read both, P/V/R order_only, V/S/W
# space_only, P/R/Q neither; of P/Q/R only Q is the reading-middle; over Q/R/S none is a spatial middle yet S is the reading-middle. Two endpoints in one
# group refuse SameGroup; a background tap refuses EmptyClick; an off-map point refuses PointOutOfBounds; determinism. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/click_between_witness.rish

say "click_between: Language EN -- Season G three-click betweenness; reading-order betweenness and spatial betweenness are DIFFERENT relations that differ in KIND, a bounding-box span over-claiming the between the total reading order names exactly; NO float, NO tolerance."
say "click_between: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the ternary betweenness tests over the two registers; click_order owns click_group_min_rank and click_group_id, click_bounds owns click_bbox, hit_test owns the point-to-object arbiter, overlap_clusters owns cluster_of. No plane of its own, no pixel written -- a reading over readings."
say "click_between: Lens TAME -- each click resolves to at most one label through the hit test, each rank walks the object count and each frame the group length bounded by label_max_pixels; two endpoints in one group refuse SameGroup (no interval), a background tap refuses EmptyClick, a point off the map refuses PointOutOfBounds having read nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/click_between"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/click_between.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "click_between: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "click_between: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "click_between: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-click-between" else "click_between: selftest did not print the GREEN line"
assert selftest.out contains "the THREE-CLICK BETWEENNESS relation" else "click_between: the three-click-betweenness claim did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "reading-order betweenness and spatial betweenness are DIFFERENT relations" else "click_between: the decisive crux did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "ORDER_ONLY" else "click_between: the order_only verdict did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "SPACE_ONLY" else "click_between: the space_only verdict did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "TOTALITY OF THE READING MIDDLE" else "click_between: the totality claim did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "NO SPATIAL MIDDLE AT ALL" else "click_between: the no-spatial-middle claim did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "refuse SameGroup by name" else "click_between: the SameGroup refusal did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "the same triple reads the same verdict twice" else "click_between: determinism did not print"

say "click_between: GREEN on metal -- the three-click betweenness relation, two endpoint taps and one middle-candidate tap resolving to three whole groups then read for betweenness in the reading sequence and in space, the two relations differing in verdict and in kind, refusals by name, determinism. Season G open-media."
